cff-version: "1.2.0"
title: "simd-ml-kernels: hand-vectorized SIMD kernels for machine learning workloads"
authors:
  - family-names: "Myet"
    given-names: "Min Htet"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mattral/simd-ml-kernels"
url: "https://zenodo.org/records/20616502"
abstract: >
  C++17 library of hand-vectorized x86 kernels for GEMM (FP32, FP16, BF16
  and INT8), decode GEMV, ggml Q8_0 and Q4_0 GEMV, and GeLU, ReLU, SiLU,
  softmax and LayerNorm, with Python bindings. Every kernel has a portable
  scalar path. AVX2 covers every kernel. AVX-512 covers the FP32, FP16 and
  BF16 GEMMs and the decode GEMV. AVX-VNNI and AVX512-VNNI cover INT8 GEMM
  and the Q8_0 and Q4_0 GEMVs. Opt-in AVX512-BF16 dot covers packed BF16
  GEMM. The Zenodo preprint describes the earlier AVX2 kernels; current
  scope and results are in the repository README.
keywords:
  - simd
  - avx2
  - avx-512
  - avx-vnni
  - gemm
  - gemv
  - machine-learning
  - microkernels
  - gelu
  - layer-normalization
  - cpp
preferred-citation:
